module generic_call.pos_2

// DEDUCTION FROM THE ARGUMENTS: the same body instantiated twice with NO
// turbofish anywhere (E2-b3 wave 1, donor Go 1.18 argument-directed inference).
//
// Two instances on purpose. A fixture calling `dbl(21)` alone would pass while
// the deduction always answered "int" -- the weak-fixture class (registry
// #465). Here the second call must deduce f64, and the body's `+` differs by
// type: on int it is the checked helper, on f64 the raw C operator. A
// deduction that silently answered int for both would print a different number.
//
// Measured when the wave landed (2026-08-23): the emission of this file is
// BYTE-IDENTICAL to the same file with `dbl[int]`/`dbl[f64]` written out, which
// is the point -- deduction writes into the same channel the turbofish writes
// into, so mono cannot tell the two apart and no second source of truth exists.
fn dbl[T](x T) -> T => x + x

fn main() {
    println(dbl(21))
    println(dbl(1.5))
}
